SpendBranch Source-Available Audit License, version 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 SpendBranch. All rights reserved.

This repository is public so that anyone can inspect, in full, the software
that SpendBranch asks them to install on their machine. It is source-available
for auditing. It is NOT open source software.

1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means everything in this repository: source code, schemas, test
fixtures, build and CI configuration, and documentation.

"SpendBranch" means the owner of this repository and its authorized
representatives.

"Official Binary" means an executable built and distributed by SpendBranch
through the channels SpendBranch designates for that purpose.

"Audit Purpose" means inspecting, verifying, testing or researching the
Software in order to understand what it does, to assess its security and
privacy properties, or to confirm that an Official Binary corresponds to this
source code.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

You may, free of charge and for an Audit Purpose only:

a. view, read, search and analyze the Software, including with automated
   analysis tools;
b. download an unmodified copy of the Software, build it unmodified on your own
   machines, and run its tests and the resulting build, solely to carry out the
   audit (including comparing the result with an Official Binary);
c. quote short excerpts of the Software, with attribution, in security
   reports, research, reviews and technical discussion;
d. report issues, vulnerabilities and suggestions to SpendBranch.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Except as SpendBranch expressly permits in writing, you may not:

a. use the Software, or anything derived from it, for any commercial purpose,
   or in any product or service, whether or not you charge for it;
b. fork the Software, or create any derivative work from it;
c. modify, adapt, translate, port or patch the Software, other than the
   temporary, local, unredistributed changes strictly needed to run an audit
   (for example, adding logging to observe behavior), which you must discard
   when the audit ends;
d. copy, publish, host, distribute, sublicense, sell, lease or otherwise make
   the Software available to anyone else, in source or binary form, in whole
   or in part (other than the excerpts allowed in section 2c);
e. run or deploy a build you made yourself as a substitute for an Official
   Binary, or offer one to others;
f. remove or alter any copyright, license or attribution notice;
g. use the SpendBranch name, logos or marks to endorse or promote anything
   without permission.

Using an Official Binary is governed by the terms under which SpendBranch
provides it, not by this license.

4. GITHUB AND OTHER HOSTING PLATFORMS

The terms of a hosting platform may let users view or fork public
repositories using that platform's features. Those platform features do not
grant you any license to the Software beyond this license. A fork made with a
platform feature is still subject to this license, and sections 3b and 3d
still apply to it.

5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This license covers only the material SpendBranch owns. Third-party
dependencies are not part of the Software; each one stays under its own
license.

6. FEEDBACK

If you send SpendBranch feedback, suggestions or reports, SpendBranch may use
them without restriction and without any obligation to you.

7. NO RIGHTS BEYOND THIS LICENSE

SpendBranch keeps all rights not expressly granted here. No patent license is
